Project Overview 
FinGrator Pulse – Project Brief (300 words) 
FinGrator Pulse is a next-generation financial intelligence platform designed to help 
individuals better understand, manage, and improve their financial lives. Unlike traditional 
budgeting apps that focus only on tracking expenses, Pulse combines real-time data, 
predictive analytics, and decision-support tools to enable users to make smarter financial 
choices and build long-term financial health. 

At its core, FinGrator Pulse integrates data from multiple sources such as bank accounts, 
mobile money wallets (e.g., MTN MoMo), SMS alerts, emails, and uploaded statements. This 
allows the app to automatically track income, expenses, and cash balances without requiring 
manual input. Transactions are categorized using intelligent rules, giving users a clear view of 
where their money is coming from and how it is being spent. 

A key feature of Pulse is its Cash Flow Engine, which analyzes historical inflows and 
outflows and forecasts future financial positions. Based on this, the app generates a Pulse 
Score (green, yellow, or red) to indicate the user’s current and future financial health. The 
app also identifies potential shortfalls, helping users anticipate when they may run out of 
money. 

FinGrator Pulse includes a What-If Simulation (Pulse Lab), where users can test financial 
decisions such as reducing spending, increasing income, or investing regularly. It also offers 
Investment Projections, showing how small, consistent contributions can grow over time, 
and Financial Readiness Tools for goals such as buying a car or a home. 
To drive engagement, Pulse incorporates gamification features such as progress tracking, 
savings goals, and financial health improvements. Additionally, users can access financial 
advisory services, either through AI-driven insights or by booking sessions with human 
advisors. 

Overall, FinGrator Pulse aims to move users from financial uncertainty to clarity, control, and 
long-term wealth creation. 

